  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promouvoir le dveloppement de la Riziculture dans la plaine de Bugarama</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KOIMUNYA is a ooperative of rice farmers growing rice in the Bugarama lowlands in Rusizi District, Western Province of Rwanda. It is an area very favorable to rice growing. The 2,362 farmers produce good quantities of paddy, but far from being enough to supply the five rice processing factories in their area. Moreover, the infrastructures that the cooperative members use are very old and not enough, taking into account the current production quantities, which they plan to even increase further. Lack of transport means also hinders the smooth collection of paddy, which in addition has a negative impact on quality and quantity (post-harvest losses). Being a certified seed multiplier, KOIMUNYA lacks enough budget to take advantage of that facility. They wish to be given support to address these challenges and take advantage of that unsatisfied market (5 factories to supply). KOIMUNYA is the largest cooperatve in the area.</narrative>
  </description>
